<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.3.5: Describe Mathematically Changes in Growth</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01271</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.3.5: Describe Mathematically Changes in Growth</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ca07d5b2-a91a-4f2a-906c-6ca0270fdf5b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title> Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>The tables show the cat population on two islands over several years. Describe mathematically, as precisely as you
  can, how the cat population on each island is changing.</para>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">year</entry>
      <entry>
        0
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">number of cats on Meow Island</entry>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        6
      </entry>
      <entry>
        18
      </entry>
      <entry>
        54
      </entry>
      <entry>
        162
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> </para>
<list>
  <item> tripling each year </item>
  <item> growing by a common ratio each year </item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead/>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">year</entry>
      <entry>
        0
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">number of cats on Purr Island</entry>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        6
      </entry>
      <entry>
        10
      </entry>
      <entry>
        14
      </entry>
      <entry>
        18
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis></para>
<list>
  <item> adding 4 cats each year </item>
  <item> characterized by a common difference each year </item>
</list>
<title>Response to Student Thinking</title>
<title> More Chances</title>
<para>Students will have more opportunities to understand the mathematical ideas in this cool-down, so there is no need to
  slow down or add additional work to the next lessons. Instead, use the results of this cool-down to provide guidance
  for what to look for and emphasize over the next several lessons to support students in advancing their current
  understanding.</para></section>
</content>
